      "correct_option": "B",
      "explanation": "\u222b\u2080\u00b9(x\u00b2+1)dx = [x\u00b3/3 + x]\u2080\u00b9 = (1/3 + 1) - 0 = 4/3."
    },
    {
      "id": "P23_M2",
      "topic": "Inverse Trigonometric Functions",
      "sub_topic": "Identities",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "If tan^{-1}(x) + tan^{-1}(y) = \u03c0/4, and xy < 1, then x + y + xy equals:",
      "options": [
        "A) 2",
        "B) -1",
        "C) 1",
        "D) 0"
      ],
      "correct_option": "C",
      "explanation": "Using tan^{-1}(x) + tan^{-1}(y) = tan^{-1}((x+y)/(1-xy)) = \u03c0/4. So (x+y)/(1-xy) = 1, giving x+y = 1-xy, so x+y+xy = 1."
    },
    {
