      "topic": "Relations and Functions",
      "sub_topic": "Inverse of a Function",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "If f(x) = (2x + 1)/(x - 3), then f^{-1}(x) equals:",
      "options": [
        "A) (x + 1)/(2x - 3)",
        "B) (3x + 1)/(x - 2)",
        "C) (x - 3)/(2x + 1)",
        "D) (3x - 1)/(x + 2)"
      ],
      "correct_option": "B",
      "explanation": "y = (2x+1)/(x-3) \u27f9 y(x-3) = 2x+1 \u27f9 yx - 3y = 2x+1 \u27f9 x(y-2) = 3y+1 \u27f9 x = (3y+1)/(y-2). So f^{-1}(x) = (3x+1)/(x-2)."
